	LispView Interface for the XView Ttysw Module 


This interface is just a thinly disguised LispView version of the
XView Ttysw or TTY package.  The names/semantics of the TTY attributes
have not been changed, the O'Reilly "XView Programming Manual" 
should be used as a reference.  

For each attribute that supports it there is a make-instance initarg,
a reader method, and a setf method.  Note that when a LispView
attribute is used as an initarg the "tty-" prefix is dropped, e.g. the
initarg for tty-left-margin would be :left-margin.  The type
argv-sequence is a sequence of strings (without a terminating NULL at
the end of the sequence), this is a Lisp version of the C argument
vector.

The accessors for attributes whose type is boolean are non standard:
the reader always returns NIL or T even if the attribute has been set
to a non nil value other than T.  This was done to avoid the overhead
required to cache Lisp values for each boolean attribute.


LispView Attribute        XView Attribute           Type            Usage
------------------        ---------------           ----            -----
tty-left-margin           XV_LEFT_MARGIN            (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-right-margin          XV_RIGHT_MARGIN           (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-bottom-margin         XV_BOTTOM_MARGIN          (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-top-margin            XV_TOP_MARGIN             (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-margin                XV_MARGIN                 (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-rows                  WIN_ROWS                  (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-columns               WIN_COLUMNS               (integer 0 *)   initarg, accessor
tty-font                  XV_FONT                   font            initarg, accessor
tty-console               TTY_CONSOLE               boolean         initarg, writer
tty-argv                  TTY_ARGV                  argv-sequence   initarg
tty-argv-do-not-fork      TTY_ARGV_DO_NOT_FORK      argv-sequence   initarg
tty-page-mode             TTY_PAGE_MODE             boolean         initarg, accessor
tty-pid                   TTY_PID                   integer         initarg, accessor
tty-quit-on-child-death   TTY_QUIT_ON_CHILD_DEATH   boolean         initarg, writer
tty-tty-fd                TTY_TTY_FD                integer         reader



BUGS/LIMITATIONS

- The build.lisp file for the tty software should be loaded BEFORE starting the
notifier process, i.e. before making an instance of a LV:display.  Actually
it's only really neccessary to load the notifier file early.

- According to the "Revised for Version 2" XView programming manual (bottom of
page 210), "you can have only one tty subwindow per process".  Additionally it
appears that you can not destroy your one tty window and then create another.

- There's probably not much Lisp applications can do with tty-pid.
